# **3.  Chip ****&**** Badge Color System — v36.3 Design Standard**

All chips, pills, and badges site-wide follow a single semantic color vocabulary. Color encodes meaning — not workspace, not feature. Eight roles, one color each. All chips use a 2px border (updated v36.2).

| **Role** | **CSS Class** | **Color** | **Hex** | **When to Use** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Freeman Now | .chip-now | Cobalt | #C2D8F8 / #1A40A6 | Freeman Now platform identifier only. |
| Freeman Next | .chip-info | Cyan | #00BDF6 | Freeman Next platform, workspace/topic labels, informational category chips. |
| Success / Complete | .chip-green | Green | #42BB37 | Task complete, plan confirmed, on track, approved, positive lifecycle event. |
| Due Next / KPI Near | .chip-amber | Gold | #FFB500 | Next step in process (no deadline), KPI Near Goal, attention items. |
| Due Today / Urgent | .chip-urgent | Orange | #FB471F | Task due today, Action Required, Rejected/Denied outcomes. |
| Overdue / KPI Below | .chip-overdue | Deep Red | #C0001A | Past deadline, KPI Below Goal. Intentionally non-brand for clarity. |
| Location | .chip-location | Fuchsia | #FF0373 | Branch, region, or scope on Needs Attention cards. Location only. |
| Stage / Phase / Type | .chip-stage | Ghost | transparent | Pipeline stages, phases, type labels, attributes. |

# **4.  Needs Attention Card Structure — Universal Rule**

Every card in the Needs Attention panel follows the same structure regardless of source workspace. All three home page columns (Active Events, Needs Attention, Customer Resolution) use a fixed 110px card height with justify-content: space-between and CSS ellipsis truncation on meta lines.

- Title: specific task or action name (not the workspace name). White-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis.

- Supporting line: task description if one exists, blank if not. Truncated to one line with … if longer.

- Status pill: Due Next (amber) → Due Today (orange) → Overdue (red). Priority wins. One pill only.

- Topic pill: workspace name in cyan (Recruiting, Onboarding, Timekeeping, etc.)

- Location pill: branch or scope in fuchsia (Nashville, Enterprise, Las Vegas, etc.)

- Chip rows use flex-wrap: nowrap so chips never break to a second line.

# **5.  Active Events Card Structure — v36.6 Design Standard**

- Title row: Show name + separator + Job # (cyan, bold).

- Meta line (single): Venue/facility · Date range (May 13 – May 20) · Booth count. All on one line with ellipsis truncation.

- Platform chip: Freeman Now (cobalt) or Freeman Next (cyan).

- No branch/producing branch shown on the card. Location context comes from the venue name.

- Date format: "Mon DD – Mon DD" with en-dash. No "Move-in" or "Clear" labels.

# **6.  KPI Tile Design — v36.13 Design Standard**

KPI sidebar tiles (left panel of the KPIs workspace) display each metric's name, current value, goal, and performance status. The progress bar and inline colored status text were replaced in v36.13 with a cleaner pill-based layout.

| **Element** | **Specification** |
| --- | --- |
| Metric name | Uppercase, bold, muted gray. Top of card. |
| Current value | Large (28px bold), Freeman Blue (#001F5F). Dominant visual. |
| Goal label | "Goal: X%" — regular weight, muted gray (#7A8099). Not bold. |
| Status pill | Floated right on the goal line. Color-coded: green (Exceeds Goal), gold (Meets Goal), red (Below Goal). No arrows. No progress bar. |
| Progress bar | Removed in v36.13. |

# **7.  Recruiting ****&**** Hiring — ES Date Gate (v36.10)**

The hiring cycle for all open positions is controlled by two enterprise-level dates set by Craig Gaibler or Nesana Wieger: the next ES Start Date and the next ES NET Class date. These are not per-hire checklist items — they are the starting gun that unlocks all open positions simultaneously.

## **How the cycle works**

- Open positions accumulate on the Recruiting & Hiring board as roles become available (offboards, transitions, new approvals). They are visible but frozen.

- While either date is TBD, every position's checklist shows a locked state: padlock icon + "Awaiting confirmed start dates."

- Craig or Nesana clicks "Set Next ES Start Date" or "Set Next ES NET Class" in their Needs Attention panel and enters a date via modal. These reminders appear automatically when both dates are blank.

- The moment both dates are confirmed, all frozen positions unlock simultaneously. Each position's first task routes to the appropriate hiring manager.

- Three weeks after the NET Class date passes, both dates automatically reset to TBD. This re-triggers the reminders for Craig and Nesana, starting the next cycle.

## **Architecture**

- t0a (Set Next ES Start Date) and t0b (Set Next ES NET Class) are enterprise-level triggers only. They are NOT included in any hire record's task checklist or TASK_STAGE_MAP.

- renderNeedsAttention() checks esDateGet('start') and esDateGet('net') directly. If either is TBD, Craig/Nesana see frozen position cards. Regular hiring managers see nothing until their positions unlock.

- renderDetail() gates the checklist the same way — frozen state shown instead of tasks when dates are TBD.

- The saveEsDate() sync logic that previously pushed t0a/t0b checkmarks onto individual hire records has been removed.

# **8.  Pop-Up Modal System — v36.7 Design Standard**

All modal/popup windows across the ES Command Center follow a unified two-component system. Every modal uses the same structural template — differing only in content, field configuration, and button color intent.

## **Universal Modal Rules**

| **Rule** | **Value** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Width | 460px | One standard width for all modals. max-width: 96vw for small screens. |
| Header | #001F5F cobalt | White title (15px bold) + muted subtitle (12px, 65% opacity white). |
| Overlay tint | rgba(0,31,95,.5) | Cobalt-tinted backdrop. Consistent with Freeman brand. |
| Field inputs | border-radius: 999px | Full pill shape on all inputs and selects. |
| Cancel button | Ghost pill | Transparent bg, 1.5px border, Freeman Blue text. Always left of primary. |
| Submit button | #42BB37 green pill | Used for all standard save/submit/open/initiate/complete actions. |
| Destructive button | #FB471F orange pill | Used only for reject/delete actions. Accompanied by warning banner. |
| Warning banner | Orange pill banner | Shown above the form in destructive modals: "This action cannot be undone." |

## **Modal Inventory**

| **Modal** | **Workspace** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Open a Position | Recruiting & Hiring | Subtitle: "Recruiting & Hiring". Standard form modal. |
| Open a Transition | Transitions / Offboarding | Subtitle: "Transitions & Offboarding". Type toggle (Promotion / Transfer) is pill-shaped. |
| Initiate Performance Action | Performance Management | Subtitle: "Performance Management". Error banner uses pill shape. |
| Set Deadline | Performance Management | Subtitle: dynamic — e.g. "Mid-Year Discussion · Performance Management". |
| Set ES / NET Date | Recruiting & Hiring | Subtitle: dynamic from calling context. Radio + inline date input pattern. |
| Reject Candidate | Recruiting & Hiring | Subtitle: "Role — Branch". Destructive modal. Static HTML (not JS-constructed). |
| Complete Staffing Process | Staffing | Subtitle: "Show Name · Job #N". Numbered step summary. Green Complete button. |

# **9.  Timekeeping ****&**** Utilization — Reporting-Structure Visibility Logic**

Introduced in v36.1. The T&U workspace is gated by reporting structure, not by title. A leader sees the workspace only if they have at least one qualifying direct report in TEAM_MEMBERS.

## **Qualifying direct report titles**

- Exhibitor Services Specialist

- Exhibitor Services Sr Specialist

- Exhibitor Services Consultant

- Exhibitor Services Coordinator (see VP exception below)

- Exhibitor Services Event Experience Supervisor

- Exhibitor Services Sr Event Experience Supervisor

- Exhibitor Services Training Supervisor

## **VP Exception — title-based rule**

A Vice President does not manually approve timecards for hourly direct reports. VPs are exempt from all timecard-approval tasks (k1, k2, k4, k5, k6, wf1–wf4). They retain only non-approval tasks. An Exhibitor Services Coordinator reporting directly to a VP does not count as a qualifying direct report.

## **Resulting visibility by role**

| **Leader** | **Title** | **T****&****U Visibility** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Craig Gaibler | Sr Director | Hidden — only RDs report to him |
| Nesana Wieger | Vice President | Hidden — VP exception applies |
| Cory Marin | Director | Hidden — only Managers report to him |
| Jennifer Vaughan | Regional Director | Hidden — only Directors report to her |
| Leslie Davis | Regional Director | Hidden — only Managers/Directors report to her |
| Lubi Garza | Regional Director | Hidden — only Directors report to him |
| Lisette Bergeron | Regional Director | Hidden — only Directors report to her |
| Ellen Crowley | Regional Director | Visible — has 9 ICs as direct reports |
| Maud Langlois | Regional Director | Visible — has Consultants + Specialist as direct reports |
| All Managers | Manager | Visible — always have qualifying direct reports |
| Most Directors | Director | Visible — most have qualifying direct reports |

# **10.  Birthday Cards — Today's Priorities Needs Attention**

Birthday cards appear in the Needs Attention column on Today's Priorities for any team member in the current identity's full reporting chain whose birthday matches today's date.

## **Card design — Option A**

| **Element** | **Value** |
| --- | --- |
| Title | 🎂 [Name]'s Birthday |
| Meta line | [Month Day] · [Job Title] |
| Status chip | "Today" (chip-urgent / orange) |
| Location chip | Branch or region (chip-location / fuchsia) |
| No workspace chip | Not shown — birthday is self-explanatory |
| Click action | Navigates to Team Members lens with name pre-filled in search |

## **Reporting chain logic**

A leader sees birthday cards for anyone in their full chain: direct reports (mgr field), their managers' reports (mgr2), and the level below that (mgr3). Uses flat field lookup — no recursive traversal needed since chain is already encoded in TEAM_MEMBERS.

## **Window**

Today only. No lookahead. A card appears only on the exact birthday date.

## **Data notes**

248 of 274 TEAM_MEMBERS records have birthday data. 26 are blank — these will never generate a card until the field is populated. Format is "Mon DD" (e.g. "May 23"). No birth year stored.

# **11.  Key Functions Reference**

| **Function** | **Purpose** |
| --- | --- |
| **buildIdentityFromTM(tm)** | Derives level, taskRole, canCheckOwner, regions, branches from a TEAM_MEMBERS record. |
| **currentIdentity()** | Returns the active identity object. |
| **setIdentity(key)** | Switches active identity, updates nav visibility, re-renders active page. |
| **tkIsVisible()** | Returns true if current identity has qualifying direct reports. Gates T&U workspace. |
| **esDateGet(type)** | Returns current ES Start Date or NET Class date. Returns "tbd" if not yet set. |
| **esDateIsEditable()** | Returns true only for Craig/Nesana identities. Gates the date-setting modals. |
| **renderNeedsAttention()** | Builds all NA cards. RH block gates on ES dates. T&U block wrapped in tkIsVisible() gate. |
| **renderDetail()** | Renders hire record detail panel. Shows frozen state ("Awaiting confirmed start dates") if ES dates are TBD. |
| **renderActiveEvents()** | Renders Active Events column cards from getScopeShows(). |
| **kpiStatusLabel(status)** | Returns "Exceeds Goal", "Meets Goal", or "Below Goal" (no arrows). Used in KPI sidebar pills. |

