# **14.  Global Design Rules — Non-Negotiable**

| **Rule** | **Detail** |
| --- | --- |
| **No strikethrough — ever** | Completed tasks, done states, and checked items are NEVER shown with strikethrough text (text-decoration:line-through). Done states are indicated by muted color (var(--muted)) and a filled green checkbox only. This applies to every workspace, every task list, every process step, site-wide, without exception. |
| **No color-coded identity cards for TR/OFF** | Transitions and Offboarding identity cards use Freeman Blue (var(--mb)) for the top bar, avatar, and progress bar — same as RH, OB, PM, and Staffing. No gold or orange accent colors on identity cards. Color-coded chips are acceptable, but structural card elements are always blue. |
| **No overdue tracking on TR/OFF** | Transitions and Offboarding are open-ended sequential workflows with no per-step deadlines. Overdue date calculations do not apply. Track chip shows "In Progress" or "Complete" only. Overdue tracking is exclusive to Recruiting & Hiring where date-anchored deadlines are meaningful. |
| **Task layout: Option A** | On Offboarding (and any future process page that has both descriptions and links): task title on top, brief description below it, "Additional details ↗" pill on its own line underneath the description. Never inline, never between title and description. |
| **Task descriptions: no "the", use "&" not "and"** | All task description copy follows these two rules: remove unnecessary "the" articles; replace "and" with "&". Keeps descriptions concise and scannable. |
| **Section labels on all pages** | Every page in the site begins its content area with an el-section-div label. Employee Lifecycle and Team Operations pages use "[Page Name] by the Numbers". Lens pages use "[Lens Name] Search". This matches the "Welcome" label on Today's Priorities and "Current KPIs" on the KPIs page. |
| **No page subtitles** | Page subtitles removed site-wide in v36.32 — redundant with page title and scope pills. Coming Soon pages and the Today's Priorities date stamp are exceptions. updateAllSubtitles() retained as no-op. |
| **Dynamic scope subtitles on all filtered pages** | Every page affected by the scope filter pills (Enterprise / Region / Branch) displays a dynamic subtitle that appends "— [scope]" to the page name or description. Subtitle updates on scope change, page navigation, and app init via updateAllSubtitles(). Lens pages are excluded (not scope-filtered). |
| **Sequential process rule — Today's Priorities** | Needs Attention cards on Today's Priorities follow strict sequential logic: only the globally-next unchecked task in a process record surfaces a card, and only to the identity who owns that exact step. No cards surface for steps blocked by incomplete prior steps, regardless of ownership. This applies to RH (needsMyAction), OB/TR/OFF (lcNeedsAction), and the RH NA render block. |
| **Page structure validation before every push** | All code changes are validated for (1) JS syntax via node Function() parse and (2) HTML div balance across all 20 page divs before being committed. A broken div balance causes all pages to bleed into each other. |

